+`devhost.toml` reads the Storybook hostname from the `DEVHOST_STORYBOOK` environment variable through devhost's `{{ env.DEVHOST_STORYBOOK }}` interpolation, for both `services.storybook.host` and `services.storybook.env.__VITE_ADDITIONAL_SERVER_ALLOWED_HOSTS`. devhost refuses to load the manifest when the variable is undefined.
+
+The committed `.envrc` sets `DEVHOST_STORYBOOK="shadcn.localhost"` and then loads an optional, untracked `.envrc.local`. With [direnv](https://direnv.net/), allow the file once with `direnv allow`. To use another hostname, export `DEVHOST_STORYBOOK` in `.envrc.local`; keep private hostnames there rather than in tracked files. Without direnv, export the variable in the shell that runs devhost.
 
